// Regression case for the build_pattern divergence (NOT fixed by fc46e9db):
// an out-of-range `\xHH` escape inside a `like` pattern must be a parse error,
// exactly as Cedar rejects it. Cedar's `\x` accepts only 0x00-0x7F, so it
// rejects `like "\xFF"` with `the input \xFF is not a valid escape`.
//
// The current build_pattern does not recognize `\x` at all: it emits `x`, `F`,
// `F` as ordinary pattern characters, so the policy parses and validates
// cleanly. This pins the reject half of the `\x` gap for patterns.
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when { context.input.document like "\xFF" };
